STEP 9 — authApi.js

Create:

frontend/src/redux/authApi.js

This is the main RTK Query file.

import { createApi, fetchBaseQuery } from "@reduxjs/toolkit/query/react";

export const authApi = createApi({
  reducerPath: "authApi",

  baseQuery: fetchBaseQuery({
    baseUrl: "http://localhost:5000/api/auth",
  }),

  endpoints: (builder) => ({

    register: builder.mutation({
      query: (userData) => ({
        url: "/register",
        method: "POST",
        body: userData,
      }),
    }),

    login: builder.mutation({
      query: (userData) => ({
        url: "/login",
        method: "POST",
        body: userData,
      }),
    }),

  }),
});


export const {
  useRegisterMutation,
  useLoginMutation,
} = authApi;
RTK Query இதுல என்ன செய்கிறது?

Normally:

fetch("http://localhost:5000/api/auth/login")

நாம் manually எழுதுவோம்.

RTK Query-ல்:

login: builder.mutation({

API define செய்கிறோம்.

Then Login page:

const [loginUser] = useLoginMutation();

Then:

loginUser({
  email,
  password
});

That's it. 👍

STEP 10 — store.js

Create:

frontend/src/redux/store/store.js

Code:

import { configureStore } from "@reduxjs/toolkit";
import { authApi } from "../authApi";

export const store = configureStore({

  reducer: {
    [authApi.reducerPath]: authApi.reducer,
  },

  middleware: (getDefaultMiddleware) =>
    getDefaultMiddleware().concat(authApi.middleware),

});
Explanation
configureStore

English: Creates Redux store.

Tamil: Redux central store உருவாக்குகிறது.

authApi.reducer

English: Adds RTK Query data to Redux.

Tamil: RTK Query data Redux store-க்கு connect ஆகிறது.

authApi.middleware

English: Enables RTK Query API features.

Tamil: RTK Query requests/cache/loading போன்ற features work ஆக middleware தேவை.

