              </p>

            </div>


            <div className="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow">

              <h2 className="text-xl font-bold mb-2">
                Reports
              </h2>

              <p className="text-gray-600">
                View reports
              </p>

            </div>


          </div>

        </div>

      </main>


      <Footer />

    </div>
  );
}

export default Home;
STEP 18 — index.css

If you're using Tailwind already, keep your existing Tailwind setup.

For basic version:

@import "tailwindcss";

If your current Tailwind project is already working, don't change your Tailwind configuration unnecessarily.

STEP 19 — App.css

You can keep:

#root {
  min-height: 100vh;
}
STEP 20 — Frontend package install

Frontend terminal:

cd fullstack/frontend

Run:

npm install

If RTK packages not installed:

npm install @reduxjs/toolkit react-redux

React Router:

npm install react-router-dom
STEP 21 — Run Frontend

Frontend terminal:

npm run dev

You'll get something like:

Local: http://localhost:5173/

Open:

http://localhost:5173
STEP 22 — Run BOTH terminals

This is very important.

Terminal 1 — Backend
cd fullstack/backend
npm start

You should see:

MongoDB connected
Server running on http://localhost:5000
Terminal 2 — Frontend
cd fullstack/frontend
npm run dev

You should see:

Local: http://localhost:5173/

Both must be running.

