Open:

http://localhost:5173/register

Enter:

Name:
Arun

Email:
arun@gmail.com

Password:
123456

Click:

Register

Flow:

Register.jsx
      ↓
useRegisterMutation()
      ↓
RTK Query
      ↓
POST /api/auth/register
      ↓
Express
      ↓
bcrypt
      ↓
MongoDB

You should get:

Registration successful

Then automatically:

/login
STEP 24 — Check MongoDB

Open MongoDB Compass.

Connection:

mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017

Database:

fullstackDB

Collection:

users

You should see:

name: Arun
email: arun@gmail.com
password: $2b$10$........

⚠️ Password:

123456

அப்படியே MongoDB-ல் இருக்காது.

Instead hash இருக்கும்.

That's because:

bcrypt.hash(password, 10)
STEP 25 — Test Login

Open:

http://localhost:5173/login

Enter:

Email:
arun@gmail.com

Password:
123456

Click:

Login

Flow:

Login.jsx
     ↓
useLoginMutation()
     ↓
RTK Query
     ↓
POST /api/auth/login
     ↓
Backend
     ↓
User.findOne()
     ↓
bcrypt.compare()
     ↓
Login successful
     ↓
/home

Home page:

Welcome Arun
arun@gmail.com
STEP 26 — RTK Query நம்ம project-ல் எங்கே use பண்ணியிருக்கோம்?

Only one file:

frontend
└── src
    └── redux
        └── authApi.js

இதுல:

register: builder.mutation()

and:

login: builder.mutation()
Register.jsx
useRegisterMutation()
Login.jsx
useLoginMutation()

That's enough for this simple RTK Query project.

